    "intro": {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The quality climb measures how well a fixed AI writer documents this codebase with the docs tools. Each climb changes the viewer or the writer to raise the judges' scores. UI Hill Climb, a local tool repo at "
        },
        {
          "insert": "codebases/codecaine/tools/ui-hill-climb",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", runs every climb. This repo keeps the 2 parts that the tool calls: the writer in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evals/quality-climb/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and the adapter in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "hill-climb/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "h-what": {
      "id": "h-what",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "What the Climb Is"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "what-lead": {
      "id": "what-lead",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A climb starts from a run package that Ford approves. A run package is the file that names the target, its states, its criteria, its judge ladder and its briefs. Each round runs 5 steps in order."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "what-outline": {
      "id": "what-outline",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Hill Climb Round",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Write or Reuse the Pages",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "On a writer round, the adapter's writer writes each brief's page again"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "On a viewer round, the round renders the pages of the last kept writer round, or the frozen pages"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The seed points each page at this checkout's themes and unpacks the brief sources that the judges lack"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Serve the Pages",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "hill-climb/serve.ts exports each page with this checkout's viewer and serves the sites on a free port"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Screenshot Each State",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "The tool screenshots each state of each brief, in each theme and in each width that the state takes"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Judge Each Page",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Each judge on the board gives each criterion one score per screenshot, and scores the 8 page categories"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Gate the Round",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Each judge on the board must reach a set mean of 9.5 on each criterion, on both sets, with no page under 9.0"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "what-builder": {
      "id": "what-builder",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Between rounds, the builder, Claude Opus 5.5 at high effort, makes one viewer or writer change. It works in its own git repo, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<run>-builder/worktree",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and reads findings for the climb set only. The held-out set then shows whether a change helps pages it was not made for. The driver keeps a change when its gate passes or its climb score stays at or above the last kept round's."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "what-judges": {
      "id": "what-judges",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The 6 judges are GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Astra, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Fable 5.2, Kimi K3.1 Pro and Muse Wonder Full 1.0. The run package's ladder puts them in rungs. A round at rung n scores with the judges of that rung and every rung below it. A run never moves down a rung."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
